  "sport": "soccer",
  "title": "Miss and you go in goal",
  "description": "One goal with a goalkeeper and a shooting line between two cones, 8–12 metres from the goal depending on age. The other players queue behind the line. The coach stands to the side with the balls and gives the next shooter a ball.\n\nThe shooter shoots from the line. A goal gives the goalkeeper a mark, and the goalkeeper stays in. A save means it is the next shooter's turn. If the shot goes wide or over, the shooter goes in goal and the goalkeeper joins the back of the queue. Marks are kept for the whole round: three marks and you rest until the round is over, and the last player left wins.\n\nAgree before you start whether rebounds count. Faster version: play with just one ball, and whoever gets the ball first after a shot runs to the line and shoots straight away. Or count goals scored instead of marks, and decide which foot and which part of the foot to use. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Pick a side of the goal before you shoot."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "A calm shot on target beats a hard one over the bar."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Standing foot beside the ball and eyes on the ball as you strike it."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "Goalkeeper: on your toes in the middle of the goal, ready to go either way."
    }
  ],
